            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p>Early Life of Hannibal Barca<br>\nHannibal Barca was born in 247 BC in the powerful city of Carthage, which is present-day Tunisia. He was born into a prestigious military family; his father, Hamilcar Barca, was a prominent Carthaginian general. From a young age, Hannibal was exposed to the military culture of Carthage and was trained in various warfare techniques. His father led him to the altar and made him swear eternal enmity toward Rome, Carthage's greatest enemy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Hannibal's Military Training</strong><br>\nHannibal's education was not like that of ordinary children; instead of playing games, he learned about war. His father took him to Spain when he was a boy, where Hannibal grew up with the soldiers and learned the art of leadership and strategy. He became fluent in several languages and was taught to endure hardship, a skill that would prove vital in his later campaigns against Rome.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Second Punic War</strong><br>\nThe Second Punic War began in 218 BC and Hannibal was ready to challenge Rome directly. He orchestrated one of the most audacious military campaigns of ancient history by marching an army, which included war elephants, across the Alps into Italy. This strategic move took the Romans by surprise and allowed Hannibal to win several significant battles on Roman soil.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
